        {
          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "This is a complex rendering engine bug related to MSAA (Multisample Anti-Aliasing) and multiple cameras rendering to the same target. Let me understand the problem:\n\n1. **Current Problem**: When multiple cameras render to the same output with MSAA enabled, only the first and last camera's contributions appear in the final image.\n\n2. **Root Cause**: Each camera has its own independent marker/flag tracking which of the two internal textures is the current main render target. This causes incorrect texture swapping between cameras.\n\n3. **Required Solution**: The active texture flag should be stored per-render-target (not per-camera), so all cameras rendering to the same target share this state.\n\nLet me first explore the codebase to understand its structure and find the relevant rendering code.\n",
