          "text": "\n\nNow I can see the issue! Looking at the code in `/workspace/crates/bevy_render/src/view/mod.rs`:\n\n1. In `prepare_view_targets` function (line 460-569), textures are cached per `(camera.target.clone(), view.hdr)` key (line 505)\n2. However, on line 557, a **new** `Arc<AtomicUsize>` is created for **each** `MainTargetTextures` entry, even when textures are reused from the cache\n3. This means each camera gets its own `main_texture` flag, causing the bug described\n\nThe fix is to store the `main_texture` flag in the cache entry itself, not in `MainTargetTextures`. Let me verify this understanding and implement the fix:\n\n",
